{
  "title": "Watch SQLite write-lock waits, WAL growth and large photo writes after the cutover",
  "description": "Every write now queues on one app-wide lock (db::write, then BEGIN IMMEDIATE), and SQLite fails a writer that waits on the file lock longer than busy_timeout (10 s, db::setup_connection). \
The pilot benchmarks (doc/sqlite-pilot-analysis.md) didn't cover photo uploads/imports (multi-MB BLOB writes inside the lock) or WAL checkpoint behavior over days of uptime. \
Add tracing for time spent waiting on the write lock and time holding it (db.rs), log any 'database is locked' error, and after a few weeks of prod use check the WAL file size and the slowest lock holders. \
Any runtime bulk job that rewrites many rows must commit in chunks.",
